        <body>
            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0938" n="844" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg844"/>

                <head>No. 492.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Connery to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 16, 1887</date>.
                        (Received November 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 273.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your No. 200, dated the 1st instant, with inclosures, relative to the case of
                    Mr. A. K. Cutting, and to say that immediately after studying it carefully in
                    connection with the exhaustive report on “Extraterritorial Crime,” I addressed
                    to Mr. Mariscal a long communication, in which I endeavored to set forth the
                    arguments embodied in your instructions why the Mexican Government should pay an
                    indemnity to Mr. Cutting, as well as modify their penal code in accordance with
                    the rules of international law.</p>
                <p>I beg to inclose herewith a copy of my note to Mr. Mariscal, from which you will
                    see that I made copious extracts from your instructions, which accounts for its
                    unusual length. I found it impossible to do otherwise without impairing the
                    force of your arguments.</p>
                <p>I trust that my communication will be found to cover all the essential points and
                    arguments, and that it will meet with your approval. I any etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas B. Conner
                    y.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d492-a1.xml" xpointer="d492-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
